"****1:54:56**** – i think this version of the code is much easier to understand:  ``` correlations = {}  for feature in selected_features:     r = pearsonr(         df_cleaned[feature],         df_cleaned['charges']     )[0]      correlations[feature] = r ```  you should try to follow a simple and readable code structure because it's much easier for beginners to understand. we don't just want to know *what* code works—we want to understand the thought process behind it. a clean structure helps us develop the right programming mindset for machine learning instead of simply copying code",neutral
