"here's how gemini summarized your video 😂: relentless self-deprecation: if you prefer high-energy or observational humor that isn't focused on personal failure, his constant focus on his own struggles with screen time (4:32), weight (4:49), and life choices might feel repetitive or depressing rather than funny. • technology cynicism: his entire set is built on a cynical view of modern tools—from labeling chatgpt as a manipulative ""yes-man"" (2:43) to describing social media algorithms as things that have him ""by the balls"" (7:31).if you are an enthusiast of al or find technology empowering, his constant bashing of these platforms might feel overly pessimistic or out of touch. • crude humor: the set includes a fair amount of edgy or vulgar language and subject matter (such as his bits about ram gopal varma camera angles (12:55) or bathroom humor). if you prefer cleaner, more lighthearted comedy, this might not be your cup of tea. • rant-style delivery: the video feels more like a stream-of-consciousness rant than a polished, tightly scripted performance. lf you prefer structured storytelling, his dritting between topics—from whatsapp stories (12:00) to courier delivery drama (15:50)—could come across as disorganized",neutral
