"i hope the arranged marriage meeting was exaggerated for laughs, but a part of me believes it could be real. it sounds funny, but imagine what the girl went through.   my aunt was searching for a bride for my cousin. he didn't object to the process, but said no to all girls seeing just a photo. it was clear he wasn't ready, but that didn't matter i guess. i was in high school back then.   one of the father insisted we come and meet them in person and my cousin was out of the country for work. my aunt was in another city and i went with my mom. she knew my cousin was not coming, but she was still in a saree and standing in a corner. this is not some village. i lived in mumbai. i was feeling so awkward. imagine how the girl must have felt.  when i grew up, i told my parents i have no issues with arranged marriage, but i will not dress up and do a fashion show. they agreed. i spoke to my now husband on the phone first. we talked and chatted for more than a month and then decided to meet. i came to chennai meet him. i went out with him alone first and then his family came to see me. by then we had already decided to get married, so it was just a meeting of families. i didn't wear a saree. didn't stand in kitchen. sat in the sofa across them and talked",neutral
