"i wonder if the ai is deleting the negative comments that may talk about how ai ""generating new content"" is already sort of an oxymoron and/or ironic statement in itself. to ""generate"" something implies it is a machine using an algorithm/calculation to mass produce stuff, while ""content"", at least in the context of media, implies some sort of art created by someone based on human emotion and passion.  ai doesn't really ""create"" content, but more rather calculates content using pattern recognition based on data it has been fed. it uses data and percentages to ""decide"" what is a ""creative"" decision, compared to how humans typically make that decision based on if they feel like it expresses their ideas/emotions the best.   ai can't really be creative, as it uses numbers and data calculations while creativity is incredibly subjective and typically based on the personal experiences of the artist. as someone who is a very logical thinker, and has trouble being ""creative"" especially when being asked to for school projects and stuff, i should definitely know lol. creativity and passion arent things you can force or teach. this applies to humans, but it especially applies to machines and ai.  please someone educate me if i'm wrong about any of this, especially if i'm wrong about my interpretation of any of these words. these are just my thoughts and opinions, which again isn't something you can really recreate with ai haha",neutral
