"the earth already has a fixed pace of time determined by its rotation and revolution, and the rate of human aging is also fixed. but..is it plausible that, like in a movie, aging would progress faster on another planet simply because its rotation and orbital speeds differ slightly? in that scene, when an actor who is unaffected by the precession and revolution periods that remained in space meets another, experiencing a temporal difference— is this really a correct scientific approach? einstein’s theory of relativity clearly contains serious errors. do not blindly believe every theory..it is merely a byproduct created by an old scientist in the past using the scientific knowledge of that time. we are people born in the future, rather than einstein, who learns and lives with greater scientific knowledge",neutral
