"cristiano amon says 2026 is a pivotal year because ai is moving from data centers into devices, cars, and factories, turning every industry into a computing and connectivity business. ​  ai beyond data centers ai is entering phones, pcs, cars, industrial systems, and robotics, creating a new phase where “everything becomes intelligent,” not just cloud servers. ​  the imf expects steady global growth partly from accelerated ai adoption, as ai becomes a strategic economic and national security priority for governments. ​  qualcomm’s strategy qualcomm positions itself as a diversified computing company, not just a mobile chip vendor, with technologies from cellular and wi‑fi to ai compute for devices and data centers. ​  the company is expanding from smartphones into automotive, industrial iot, pcs, and robotics, aiming for about half its revenue from handsets and half from these new ai‑driven sectors by fiscal 2029. ​  ai cars and robotics automakers are turning cars into “computers on wheels,” using qualcomm chips to power dashboards, connectivity, driver‑assist, and in‑car voice ai agents that let drivers talk naturally to their vehicle. ​  qualcomm is building a robotics platform for smart factories and autonomous systems, betting that ai‑driven robots and machines will be central to the future of manufacturing and industrial automation. ​",positive
