"without intelligence, autonomous ai agents are a fools game. in reality it’s a decision support tool. you can allow its probable answers to apply automatically but they must be validated for hallucinations at the least, totally inappropriate ‘decisions’ at worst. coding in theory has a closed testing loop, it may work for the immediate goal but in reality without intelligence what is created is often corner cut, technical debt. the assumption in support of market prices is that it will get better, that scaling brings agi. the models may improve against their own benchmarks but they will never be intelligent, no matter the scale or the self-training. it is an extreme theory that they can be, a very weird philosophy or even delusion created by confirmation bias sycophancy of chatting, that in my view can only at some point hit the hard walls of reality",neutral
