"it doesn't go so far as to tell us that russia thinks that ukraine thinks it would be a good idea. it only tells us that russia thinks there is a chance someone, that someone most likely being ukraine, might try it. it is more a reflection of an authoritarian leader behaving as they do with a focus on personal self defense in the context of some degree of something like both paranoia and legitimate concerns for various threats than anything else.  i wouldn't think it to be beneficial to ukraine unless very well timed around an opportunity that internal russian politics might present. if putin were facing a particularly high boiling point in sentiment against the war and an opposition had crystalized some, for instance. they'd have to be mindful that they are not going to be accomplishing a shaping operation though, nor anything else of a controlled nature. they would be trying to gauge the state of chaos in russian politics and giving it a disruptive shove at a time when it was more likely to lead to a favorably directed shift than to an unfavorably directed shift. it is not a precise maintenance operation to fix the dodgy washing machine and prevent it from making a mess everywhere. it is a kick timed when it looks like the machine will spill over away from them instead of towards them when it goes over",negative
