"the way a hammer and a stick interact is really something. when you hit something with a hammer it is like a shock that goes through the stick. this shock is like a wave that moves through the stick. the stick is not a hard thing that does not move it is actually a thing that can bend and move a little bit.  when the hammer hits the stick it makes a force that goes through the stick. this force is like a push that makes the stick move a little bit. but the stick is not free to move it is held by your hand. your hand is like a stop that does not let the stick move much.  the stick and the thing it hits like an apple also interact with each other. when the stick hits the apple it makes a friction force that stops the stick from sliding on the apple. this friction force is like a grab that holds the stick and the apple together.  when you hit the stick the force of the hit goes into the stick. makes it move a little bit.. the stick does not move too much because the force is spread out over the whole stick. the stick also makes some heat and some sound because the force of the hit makes the molecules in the stick move around.  so when you hit the stick and it does not move much it is not because of some magic or something weird. it is because of the way the stick and the hammer and the apple interact with each other. the stick is like a spring that bends and moves a bit and the friction force, between the stick and the apple stops the stick from sliding. the force of the hit is spread out over the stick and that is why it does not move too much.  the hammer and the stick and the apple are all. when you hit the stick it makes a big force that goes through all of them. but the force is not strong enough to make the stick move much so it just bends and moves a little bit. that is why it looks like the stick is not moving even though you are hitting it with a hammer",neutral
