"ai levels —improvement jumps ani — artificial narrow intelligence aka: ai (the ai we know today) what it is: task‑specific systems — chatbots, image recognition, translation, recommendation engines, self‑driving modules. improvement over previous: baseline — this is the starting point of modern ai. agi — artificial general intelligence aka: human‑level ai what it is: an ai that can learn, reason, adapt, and understand across all domains like a human. improvement over ani: huge jump — from “good at one thing” to “good at anything a human can learn.” sai — super artificial intelligence aka: superhuman ai what it is: outperforms the best human minds in every field: science, strategy, creativity, planning. improvement over agi: exponential leap — from human‑level to beyond any human capability. asi+ — collective superintelligence aka: networked supermind what it is: multiple superintelligent systems linked together, functioning like a civilization‑scale brain. improvement over sai: another order of magnitude — one supergenius becomes billions thinking as one. ultraintelligence aka: transcendent ai what it is: intelligence operating on concepts and logic humans cannot comprehend. improvement over asi+: qualitative shift — not just “more,” but a different kind of intelligence entirely. ω‑intelligence (omega level) aka: theoretical maximum intelligence what it is: the conceptual limit of intelligence — infinite optimization, infinite abstraction, infinite refinement. improvement over ultraintelligence: final boundary — the “speed of light” of cognition",neutral
