"i feel a lot of indians are debating in favour of the it companies because they are scared that ai would take their jobs. unfortunately that's true. indian it services company don't build anything meaningful, most of the work is maintenance or ktlo at best. the quality of code is sub standard, technologies used are legacy and substandard. i have seen the working ways of both service and product based companies closely and i can clearly see product based companies shifting to genai based code completion in less than 3 years (including mine). in fact, we have 4 genai based auto completion bots in production and all engineers have been asked to test which works best for them. i write more than 70% of my code through some gpt or even github copilot. i don't see any reason how service based companies could survive more than 10 years unless they dramatically pivot.   the management of such companies would have to do something truly innovative, even then i don't see a way out for employees, it's just a small hope for the companies.   kodak and blackberry were such companies that didn't move with time and collapsed even though they were building something of substance, just not relevant with time. now think of service based companies from that lens.   i sincerely hope that smart people working in such companies do scale up quickly so that they don't suffer as badly. i know the kind of things most people work on in these companies, their future looks very dark to me",negative
