"the full-scale critique ​berman reacts to massive software development agents, claiming that human programming is dead because ai can now navigate large codebases and write full scripts on the fly. this analysis is an absolute enterprise security nightmare. forcing a probabilistic model to generate unverified script loops inside an active production workspace introduces systemic instability. because these models lack a localized memory tracking loop, a single syntax error or variable misinterpretation can initiate an unmonitored recursion loop that locks up system memory and introduces backdoors. ​the tailored solution & terminal offer ​safe system automation requires a framework where complex tasks are broken down into isolated, binary verification gates. instead of allowing a probabilistic engine to write unverified script loops on the fly, every data transaction must clear a strict lateral check at the machine layer, preserving absolute system integrity. ​if you want to eliminate the extreme security risks of unverified coding agents and need total system control, contact me. i am prepared to provide you with a taste or a look at the whole architecture",negative
