"it’s a law of evolution, a law of nature: nothing specific lasts forever. human society has reached the peak of its development at a tremendous cost to itself — a cost so high that it can no longer cope with wars, ecological crises, climate change, or even demographic shifts. even less is it equipped to handle future challenges, such as a cataclysm from space that could instantly wipe out everything humanity has built as if it had never existed at all. the homo sapiens species is no longer evolutionarily viable. in its pure biological form, it is dying out. it will either be replaced by a successor — a technological species (or a hybrid techno-biological one) — or it will simply vanish. and yes — the new species that replaces humanity will operate on an entirely different level of interaction, community, and paradigms. the foundation defines the essence. just as form, in the general sense, defines content",negative
