"stock markets are at all-time highs because wealth inequality is at all-time highs.  it's not just stocks. gold, land, housing, and most other assets are also at record valuations. when an ever-growing share of wealth is concentrated in the hands of a small number of people, most of that money ends up flowing into assets, pushing prices even higher.  unless governments introduce significantly more progressive taxation or wealth taxes that slow the concentration of wealth, asset prices will keep rising because inequality will continue to widen.  for us, that increasingly means being priced out of home ownership, paying even more tax to rent services (e.g water) from private owners and to pay growing debt interest. its clear this means we will continue to face declining living standards.  the solution? tax wealth not work",neutral
