"i'm 29. graduated college at 22 and landed a contract job as a compliance analyst at a bank starting at 42k. got hired on full time after 2 years jumping up to 64k. worked very hard and got promoted to a senior analyst 2 years later jumping up to 85k. my job is very demanding and mentally exhausting. i've also been pet-sitting as a side hustle making an average of $800 per month over the last 6 years. i've lived pretty frugally and have been lucky enough to save/invest an average of 55-60% of my income. currently sitting at 138k in my individual brokerage account, 73k in my roth ira, and 34k in my 401k along with 5k in a crypto wallet and 5k in a hysa.  i have mixed feelings about where i'm at now. i know i'm in a pretty good spot financially, but i feel like i've sacrificed a lot to get here... no vacations, work life balance is not good (lots of ot needed to keep up with my current workload), pretty limited time with friends/family. i've also been single since college aside from a couple short lived flings here and there. i have a few friends that i hang out with once or twice a month.   i wouldn't say i'm verry happy. this mentality of ""work hard now enjoy life later"" has taken a toll on my mental health and i'm pretty burned out at this point. life is about balance. i think i'll continue to save and invest aggressively in my 30s and 40s, but i want to take my foot off the gas a little bit. if anyone has taken the time to read this and is in a similar spot just know that i'm proud of you. keep grinding... but try to have some fun along the way",neutral
