"i was in middle school, when the fast and the furious came out. didn't get a chance to see it in theaters, but i saw the movie on vhs. the plot and soundtrack were great, and i loved the street racing scenes. 2 fast 2 furious, the fast and the furious: tokyo drift, fast and furious 4 are also my top favorites. fast five is was a great movie, it sadly moved away from the car culture. following that movie, the writers featured one or two street racing scenes to remind the fans that they didn't forget where the franchise came from. after the 6th movie came out, that's when they started to steer off the streets and the movies became one huge ridiculous joke after another. furious 7 had los angeles, hector, race wars and a sean boswell cameo. it was really the perfect ending to fast and furious franchise. i still can't believe that we have to wait two more years to see furious 11. we were supposed to get that movie last april, but the 11th film won't be seen until the year 2028. that's five years of our lives gone and we're only getting older, not younger. some of us might be able to see the final movie and some might not. let's hope that they don't decide to push the final fast and furious movie back until 2029, that would be horrible",positive
