"i believe that the reason that drugs and talk therapy have limited affect on mental illiness is that mental illness is not an illness. it's a response. it's what a healthy brain does when it doesn't know what dangers lurk and how to protect against them. the reason mushrooms, lsd, marijuana, mdma are so good at helping fight 'mental illness' is that they break down connections in the brain and let it wire itself like it's supposed to be wired. drugs that are meant to treat depression mask wiring problems. this is just my theory and i'm not a medical professional but i do have an interest in these areas and i think that it's about wiring and reconfiguring the brain and only drugs that help do that are useful",neutral
