"kaveri is not reverse engineering, it is a new clean sheet design. also kaveri reached 50 kn dry thrust which now  matches ge 404, and 74kn afterburner  thrust which falls behind ge 404's 87 kn. this is now 80 kn in the engine being flight tested on the tejas flying testbed, which is equivalent to the 87 kn f404 after burner thrust due to the fact that the kaveri thrust is specified in hot and high conditions, whereas the ge thrust is measured at sea level low temperature conditions. what is being done now is testing and improvement for weight, durability/engine design life, and fuel efficiency. the main reason for delay other than starting from a zero technological base, is lack of funding, which is a tiny fraction of what any other country has spent on developing a new engine. india has spent $350 million on developing the kaveri so far, while india is paying saffran $7 billion for india's half of development costs for the new 120kn amca engine which is at a comparable level of technology, but larger",neutral
