"this is such a stupid explanation from a physicist. he just says “der eez-a more time here” and waves the upper watch around a little, “and a-leetle less time here” and waves the lower watch a little. no fucking non-physicist is going to have the slightest fucking clue why he’s saying that or what it means. he needs to explain that the lower watch is closer to earths gravity, and that gravity causes time dilation. so time moves slower for the watch closer to the surface of the earth because that’s where gravity is stronger. he could even use an example from a movie, like interstellar…when they land on the planet orbiting the black hole (an immensely strong gravitational field), every minute on the surface is a year on earth, which is why cooper’s daughter is suddenly in her 80s when they return, while he has hardly aged at all.  but just waving two watches and saying “more time here” means nothing to the average person. they’re gonna think he means there’s literally “more time left in the universe” higher up, or something like that. he can’t expect people to intuit general relativity on their own…. it took einstein years toi figure that out. how does a physics professor not know that he needs to explain physics to people? this is so dumb. argh",negative
