"the frustration of waiting does not instantly vanish the moment you finally arrive. instead, the lingering irritation transforms into a sharp, quiet resentment as the reality of your disrespect sets in. your arrival does not erase the time you stole. standing around for an eternity creates a psychological toll that cannot be undone by a casual hello or a weak excuse. the minutes spent checking the clock and fighting off annoyance leave a bitter aftertaste, ruining the energy of the entire meeting before it even begins. furthermore, seeing you roll up in that ridiculous, carelessly thrown-together outfit only deepens the insult. it becomes undeniable proof that you did not value this encounter enough to make an effort. your chaotic appearance shows that your delay was born out of pure indifference, forcing others to pay the price for your complete lack of discipline. the wait may technically end when you appear, but the damage to the relationship is already done. your persistent disregard for basic punctuality has officially exhausted all remaining patience, drawing a definitive line where your bad manners will no longer be tolerated",negative
