"oh, absolutely 🧐  some people have what you could call a low threshold for frustration. even tiny annoyances can trigger a strong emotional reaction—like snapping, rage, or getting “baited” easily. a few reasons why:  1. stress levels: if someone’s already stressed, even small things feel huge.   2. personality/temperament: some people are naturally more reactive.   3. sleep & diet: lack of sleep or blood sugar swings (hi sugar highs!) can make patience evaporate.   4. past experiences: if a person has trauma or frequent criticism in the past, small triggers can feel like major threats.   5. social media & environment: online, it’s easy to get “rage-baited” with trolling, clickbait, or just the constant push for reactions.    basically, the brain sometimes treats tiny annoyances as big threats, which is why some people blow up over the smallest stuff.  if you want, i can explain why getting baited actually feels kind of addictive for some people—it’s kinda wild",negative
