"bhramagupta(598–668 ce)  1)-brahmagupta(598–668 ce) contributed  arithmetic include treating zero as a number and rules for arathmatic operations involving it, such as (addition) , (subtraction) , and (multiplication).  2)-he also gave concept of negative number.   3)-brahmagupta provided formulas for calculating the sum of the squares and cubes of the first n natural numbers.   4)-he developed the formula for the area of a cyclic quadrilateral, now known as brahmagupta's formula.   5)-he introduced rules for operations with fractions and was among the first to represent fractions in a visual form similar to today's notation",neutral
"aryabhatta(476–550 ce) work on astronomy.  1)- aryabhatta gave heliocentric model.  2)- earth's rotation: aryabhata stated that the earth rotates on its own axis, which explained the apparent movement of the stars.  3)-accurate calculations: he calculated the earth's sidereal rotation to be 23 hours, 56 minutes, and 4.1 seconds, and the length of a sidereal year to be 365.25858 days, which were very close to modern values.  4)-planetary motion: he provided tables of planetary positions and calculated the speeds of planets, which were based on his heliocentric model.  5)-earth's size: he calculated the earth's circumference to be 39,968 km, which is close to the modern value.  6)-he also calculated value of pi.  7)-he calculated distance between (earth and sun) & (moon and sun).  8)- he also calculated diameter of earth, sun, moon using trigonometry",neutral
