"i've had this procedure done before, but they no longer do it in the neck (carotid artery), they do it in the groin (femoral artery). you have to be fully conscious for accurate readings, with only medicine for pain. more specifically, for when they put the catheter in. however i could still feel the needle when it went up into my brain (it obviously took a moment to get up there) and it was definitely uncomfortable. this scene gave me a bit of deja vu, not gonna lie. even the way they transfer her onto the table! also, the technician in the scene is a suspected serial killer. he was only ever convicted of one murder. the director would visit the technician while he was in prison awaiting trial for murdering a journalist, and the rumors of the technician being a serial killer of gay men is what got him interested in making the movie cruising",negative
